assistant: Subject: parse numeric epoch-ms created_at in get_order

Since vendor version 2026-10-01, `created_at` comes back as epoch milliseconds (`1792142857943`) instead of an ISO-8601 string. `get_order` ran every value through `String()` and `Date.parse()`, which can't read a numeric string. That returned `NaN`, and the `|| 0` fallback quietly turned it into 1970-01-01. The fix uses a numeric `created_at` directly as epoch milliseconds, which gives 2026-10-16T09:27Z, the time upstream sent. ISO strings from 2026-01-01 still go through the same code as before, so the v1 output is unchanged. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass, including the repro test. The tool sends the same requests as before, so the recording didn't need to change.

